From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc/rockchip: remove duplicate pm-domains driver from drivers/soc

Linux 6.5 moved the Rockchip power domain driver to drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/.
The vendor fork retained the old copy in drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c with
its own Makefile entry under the same CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_PM_DOMAINS symbol.

Both files compile and both call postcore_initcall to register a platform driver
named "rockchip-pm-domain", resulting in:

  Error: Driver 'rockchip-pm-domain' is already registered, aborting...

Remove the soc/rockchip copy from the Makefile so only the upstream
drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c is built. Neither copy has
RV1106/RV1103 power domain entries, so no functionality is lost.

---
 drivers/soc/rockchip/Makefile | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -11,7 +11,6 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_IODOMAIN) += io-domain.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_IOMUX) += iomux.o
-obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_PM_DOMAINS) += pm_domains.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_DTPM) += dtpm.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_FIQ_DEBUGGER) += fiq_debugger/
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_VENDOR_STORAGE) += rk_vendor_storage.o
